<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - CMI year attrib income drops.</title>
<headline>TABLE - CMI year attrib income drops.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Div			 20.0	  vs 90.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   54.4	  vs 177.8</p>
<p>    Operating income	31.6	  vs 185.2</p>
<p>Full name: Consolidated Metallurgical Industries Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - CMI said in a statement that it had changed its accounting policy for providing for post-retirement medical costs.</p>
<p>The firm said in a statement that its year-on-year sales volumes had jumped 19 percent but that its weighted average selling price had fallen by 33 percent. Production costs rose by seven percent.</p>
<p>The group added that results from its operations were expected to improve during the coming year but that prices are not expected to improve in the foreseeable future.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
